# This is a pnpm workspace (see packageManager in package.json). An npm command
# run from the repo root leaves a package-lock.json behind that lists nothing —
# measured at 189 bytes, naming the repo and no dependencies — and a stray one
# invites `npm install` here, which would build a flat node_modules disagreeing
# with pnpm-lock.yaml. Anchored to the root because that is where the stray
# appears; a lockfile turning up under apps/ or packages/ should stay VISIBLE.
/package-lock.json

# The browser-override config CLAUDE.md describes, and says must NEVER be
# committed: a cloud or sandbox container can carry a different Playwright
# browser build from the one the pinned @playwright/test wants, and the suite is
# pointed at the installed binary with a local config of this name. Committing it
# would pin every machine — CI included — to one absolute path under
# /opt/pw-browsers. It reached `git add -A` twice before this line existed, and a
# rule that depends on remembering it is not a rule.
apps/web/playwright.local.config.ts
playwright-report/
